        "proposal_id": "P0000",
        "source_refs": [
          "F001"
        ],
        "rationale": "In passage F001, the statute provides that 'it shall not be an unlawful employment practice' for an educational institution to hire and employ employees of a particular religion under the specified disjunctive conditions. Classifying this provision as modality 'not_required' under an exemption incorrectly cast the rule as an absence of obligation rather than an authorization to act. Changing modality to 'may' and kind to 'permission' accurately reflects the permissive modal force of declaring the practice lawful, while preserving all statutory conditions.",
        "verdict": "supported"
      },
      {
        "proposal_id": "P0001",
        "source_refs": [
          "F001"
        ],
        "rationale": "Passage F001 provides two alternative conditions connected by the disjunctive 'or': ownership, support, control, or management by a religion, 'or if the curriculum' is directed toward religious propagation. Proposal P0001 alters the summary to read 'and if the curriculum', turning alternative qualifiers into conjunctive prerequisites and improperly excluding institutions that meet only one of the statutory criteria.",
        "verdict": "unsupported"
      }
    ]
  }
